.TH LSMKINITRAMFS 1 "2026-07-15" "mkinitramfs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lsmkinitramfs \- list the contents of an initramfs image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lsmkinitramfs
.I image
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlsmkinitramfs\fP decompresses the given initramfs \fIimage\fP and lists
its contents in \fBcpio\fP verbose-table format (equivalent to
\fBcpio \-it\fP).
.PP
The compression format is detected from \fBINITFSCOMP\fP in
\fI/etc/mkinitramfs.conf\fP.  If the config file is absent or
\fBINITFSCOMP\fP is unset, \fBgzip\fP is assumed.
.PP
The tool uses \fBbsdcpio\fP(1) for listing, which must be installed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
No image argument provided, or the image could not be read.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/mkinitramfs.conf\fP
Read to determine the compression format (\fBINITFSCOMP\fP).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmkinitramfs\fP(8),
\fBmkinitramfs.conf\fP(5),
\fBbsdcpio\fP(1)
